I appreciate it and jbofi'e digests it without complaint, but what
would Poe think?&nbsp; Esperanto has over the years produced its own
literature.&nbsp; Does lojban have its great authors and poets?<br>
<br>
Thank you kindly for your effort.<br>
<br>
My response the the puzzle text you posed:<br>
.io .i'o .ui .i'e do cilre&nbsp;zo'e gi'e sarji vau la .lojban. <br>
"With respect, appreciation, delight and approval you learn and support
lojban."<br>
To the best of my beginner's understanding the denizens of selma'o UI
may be added to text more or less freely and are not bound by the
otherwise strict grammar.&nbsp; As for interpretation this seems a little
ambiguous (and therefore probably not the case).&nbsp; I've lumped them all
into one nebulous glob of attitudinal meaning.<br>
<br>
